{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-hotelling-multiyear-year-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.70, step 7f. `userdb-hotelling-multiyear-year`: `userdb-hotelling-multiyear-month` under `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>`, output Year: 2015 and 2020, a DEFAULT-domain run over the user input database `inputs/washtenaw-userdb-hotelling-multiyear.esm`. MOVESOutput is 1,952 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is AdjustHotelling.sql's pooled table under PreAggYEAR.sql: hotellingMonthAdjust is PreAggYEAR.sql's constant 1 at MonthOfAnyYear 0, numMonths is 1 and the hotellingHoursPerDay block takes its `monthID = 0` arm, and 2015's rows -- at day 0, the collapsed day -- are rescaled a second time by 2015's own block before 2020's hour and age blocks pool them (PLAN.md §7.3.66, §7.3.70).\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1 and `db_aggregationmonth` is the RunSpec's months, read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 1952, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "time-aggregation",
      "starts",
      "output-time-step",
      "idle-adjustment",
      "multi-year",
      "year-aggregation"
    ]
  },
